# The native projects ARE committed. That is deliberate.
#
# `npx cap add ios` regenerates them from a template, so it is tempting to keep
# them out and let CI run it — but everything that makes them OURS lives inside
# them: the icon set, the privacy manifest, the bundle id, the build settings,
# the signing configuration. Regenerating on every build throws all of that away
# and produces a default Capacitor app that happens to load our pages.
#
# So the projects are in git and `cap sync` (not `cap add`) is what runs in CI:
# sync copies the web build and the plugins in without touching anything else.
#
# What is ignored below is only ever produced by a build.
node_modules/

# Generated from public/ by sync-www.mjs on every build.
www/

# ---- iOS ----
ios/App/Pods/
ios/App/Podfile.lock
ios/App/build/
ios/App/output/
ios/App/App/public/
*.xcuserdatad
xcuserdata/
DerivedData/
*.mobileprovision
*.p12
*.p8

# ---- Android ----
android/.gradle/
android/build/
android/app/build/
android/local.properties
android/app/src/main/assets/public/
android/capacitor-cordova-android-plugins/build/
*.keystore
*.jks
